      "title": "What Do I Want from the Publisher of the Future?",
      "abstract": "When I took on the role of Editor-in-Chief of this open-access journal, I began, for the first time, to think about scholarly communication beyond submitting my papers and getting them published.This thinking led to previous Perspectives [1-3], all of which shared an underlying themethere are many opportunities to achieve better dissemination and comprehension of our science, and as producers of that output I believe authors have a responsibility to see it used in the best possible way.No need to take my word regarding the opportunities that exist to improve scholarly communication and comprehension.I recommend reading ''Part 4: Scholarly Communication'' from the free online book the Fourth Paradigm: Data Intensive Scientific Discovery [4] (http://research.microsoft.com/en-",
